; The Winner of the 1998 SSEM Programming Competition!
;
; Written by: 	Yasuaki Watanabe of Japan.
; Obtained from: 	The 1998 SSEM Programming Competition.
; Description: 	"This is a three minutes timer program. If you want to eat instant noodles, use this program. Start
;               the program after pour hot water into the cup. Open the cover and start to eat if the "Stop" indicator
;               is illuminated. I promise you that the noodles taste good."
; Parameter Lines: 	31: initial value for the timing interval counter. See values in code below.
; Result Lines: 	(run-time display)

00 BNUM 00000000000000000000000000000000  ; Zero word, used as a default/scratch value.
01 LDN 25                                 ; ACC = -line25.
02 STO 28                                 ; Save that value in scratch line 28.
03 LDN 28                                 ; ACC = line25.
04 SUB 29                                 ; ACC = line25 - line29: advance the display/control pattern.
05 STO 25                                 ; Store the updated display/control word back to line 25.
06 LDN 31                                 ; ACC = -timingCounter.
07 SUB 27                                 ; ACC = timingCounter - 1.
08 CMP                                    ; If the timer is negative, skip the next line.
09 JMP 26                                 ; Otherwise branch via line 26 back into the timing loop.
10 LDN 5                                  ; ACC = -line5.
11 SUB 27                                 ; ACC = line5 - 1.
12 STO 28                                 ; Save the decremented value in scratch line 28.
13 LDN 28                                 ; ACC = updated line5 value.
14 STO 5                                  ; Rewrite line 05, advancing another display/control word.
15 LDN 1                                  ; ACC = -line1.
16 SUB 27                                 ; ACC = line1 - 1.
17 STO 28                                 ; Save the decremented value in scratch line 28.
18 LDN 28                                 ; ACC = updated line1 value.
19 STO 1                                  ; Rewrite line 01, advancing the top display/control word.
20 SUB 30                                 ; Compare the updated line1 value against the stop threshold in line 30.
21 CMP                                    ; If still negative, skip the halt and continue the animation/timer.
22 STP                                    ; Stop when the display reaches the final "ready" state.
23 BNUM 00000010010000000000000000000000  ; Static display/control word.
24 BNUM 00000010001000000000000000000000  ; Static display/control word.
25 BNUM 00000000000000001111110000111111  ; Display/control word updated by lines 01-05.
26 BNUM 01100000000000000000000000000000  ; Encoded jump target used by line 09 to loop back to line 07.
27 BNUM 11111111111111111111111111111111  ; Constant -1.
28 BNUM 00000000000000000000000000000000  ; Scratch line used to hold decremented intermediate values.
29 BNUM 00000000000000000000001000111111  ; Step constant subtracted from line 25.
30 BNUM 01111011111000101111110000111111  ; Stop threshold used by line 20.
; 31 BNUM 00001011011000000000000000000001  -- timing counter for original machine
31 BNUM 01000000000000000000000000000001  ; Faster simulation timing counter.
